{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonSectorFull","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonSectorFull","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonSectorTransport","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShiftFull"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_sector","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonSectorFull.lean#L38-L55","doc":"**Watson uniqueness on the sector-at-0 (final wiring).** If `f` and `g` on\nthe sector `{z ≠ 0 : |arg z| < π/(2t)}` are the pullbacks `f = F ∘ Φ_t`,\n`g = G ∘ Φ_t` of half-plane functions `F`, `G` that agree on `{re > 0}`,\nthen `f = g` on the sector. The carrier `Φ_t(z) = (z^t)⁻¹` sends the sector\ninto `{re > 0}` (`sectorTransport_mapsTo`), so each sector point's value is\nan agreed half-plane value. Supply `hFG` from `watson_uniqueness_rhp_open`\nto obtain the full sector-at-0 Watson uniqueness. ","signatureChunk":0}]}